export default JSON.parse("{\"schema\":\"ai-brain-source-note/1.0\",\"domain\":\"studio-tools\",\"capabilities\":[\"3d\",\"canon\",\"effect\",\"galaxy\",\"generator\",\"layer\",\"lighting\",\"map\",\"mask\",\"merge\",\"npc\",\"paint\",\"planet\",\"schedule\",\"settlement\",\"simulation\",\"world\"],\"provenance\":{\"sourceGroup\":\"world-life-simulation-a\",\"sourceType\":\"provided-project-material\",\"archiveHash\":\"24ceef27ec4cc5cf\"},\"title\":\"readme.md\",\"content\":\"# WorldBuilder Setting-Agnostic Complete Edition\\n\\n## Installation\\n1. Extract `WorldBuilder.zip`.\\n2. Extract `LifeSimulation.zip` into the same parent folder and allow it to merge into the existing `WorldBuilder` folder.\\n3. Open `WorldBuilder/index.html`. For the most reliable ZIP/DOCX imports, serve the folder with any simple static web server.\\n\\nBoth archives are parts of one application. There is one shared `index.html`.\\n\\n## Six front-facing pages\\n1. Globe Editing \u2014 Continent Editor, globe/depth viewer, ZIP/project upload and world start.\\n2. Weather Editing \u2014 climate, water/tides, severe systems, atmosphere and poles.\\n3. Nearby Celestial Objects \u2014 1\u20133 moons for the main world, compound tide/weather coupling, auroras and nearby objects.\\n4. Galaxy Editing \u2014 stars, planets, orbits, retrogrades, rings, nebulae, constellations, asteroid belts, comets and distant black holes.\\n5. LifeSimulation \u2014 NPCs, locations, races, tokens, dialogue, schedules, simulation, and painterly maps/interiors.\\n6. World Lore & Systems \u2014 planet-scoped lore, transit, NPC canon, pantheons, schedules, politics, factions and data.\\n\\n## Rendering boundary\\nTrue 3D is used for planetary/world globes and galaxy/orbital visualization. Settlements, districts, caverns, underwater locations, buildings, and interiors use painterly static base art with editable layers, masks, hotspots, linked scenes, route graphs, lighting/weather effects, and schedule-driven gliding tokens.\\n\\n## Token portraits\\nThe complete folder/file tree is in `json/token_assets/`. Actual circular portrait files are expected in the GitHub repository beside the application or through a configured raw-content base URL. Missing portraits render safe labeled placeholders without breaking NPC records.\\n\\n## 2026 Painterly Map, Lighting, Weather, and Website Integration\\n\\nThis package now includes:\\n\\n- `website.html`: the long-scroll website template adapted to this project.\\n- `tools/painterly-map-lab.html`: a standalone painterly settlement, world-map, and globe generator with non-destructive weather and pseudo-3D lighting.\\n- `effects-studio/studio.html`: the full stationary-map and imported-object Visual Studio, branded for this project.\\n- A floating **Painterly & 3D Map Tools** launcher inside the primary `index.html`.\\n- Shared Google Apps Script deployment and library references supplied for this revision.\\n\\nThe map lab can export PNG and JSON, send a map to a parent program through `postMessage`, and save map metadata through the shared backend. Imported base maps remain stationary layers; lighting and weather are composited above them.\\n\"}");
